From: Marcus Schack Abildskov <work@marcus-sa.dev>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 04:59:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] spike(F2): open a block-device volume with O_EXCL
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

CH never claims a block device. Its OFD lock is keyed on the inode of the path
it opened, so a second device node for the same device (same major:minor) is
not seen as a conflict and a second VMM boots on a disk the first is writing.
O_EXCL makes the kernel arbitrate per block device (bd_prepare_to_claim,
block/bdev.c) whatever node or path names it.

Prototype for the DESIGN spikes of GH #348: typechecked, not built or run.

🤖 Generated with Claude Code

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
